Dear Managers!

=46inally, a most belated summary on a question I posed last December. The=
=20
answers came in swiftly as usual, but testing them required several 100GB o=
f=20
extra disk space, so I did not get around to it before now. And I did not=20
want to post a summary before testing myself.

My problem as that sys_check reported "Large BMT extentCnt" and "BMT pageCn=
t=20
is decreasing" on some of my AdvFS domains. =A0Advice from Rob Leadbetter a=
nd=20
Thomas Sjolshagen was as follows:

=2D Avoid having too many small files.
=2D Defragment your disk regularly, or have vfast defragment it in the=20
background continuously.
=2D If you can afford the extra diskspace, turn off the frag-file option.
You can check frag file size with

# cd /mountpoint/.tags
# ls -l 1

=2D To "cure" a domain that has huge frag files or BMT problems, get extra =
disks=20
that can hold all your data and then either

# vdump -0f - /oldmountpoint | vrestore -xf - -D /newmountpoint

or (preferred) go through an addvol/rmvol cycle (dsk4c is my regular disk,=
=20
dsk16c a temporary disk):

/usr/sbin/addvol /dev/disk/dsk16c scratch_domain=20
/usr/sbin/rmvol /dev/disk/dsk4c scratch_domain
=A0
/usr/sbin/addvol /dev/disk/dsk4c scratch_domain=20
/usr/sbin/rmvol /dev/disk/dsk16c scratch_domain=20

The first two lines moved all data to dsk16, the second moved it all back t=
o=20
dsk4. Use showfdnm to check progress. =A0This worked perfectly for me. I ke=
pt=20
users off the machine while doing this.


Best regards,
Hans E Plesser
